---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---

<Layout
	title="Terms of Use"
	description="The terms governing your use of WageLark."
>
	<div class="mx-auto max-w-[720px]">
		<h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-[var(--navy)] md:text-4xl">Terms of Use</h1>
		<p class="mt-2 text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-[var(--ink)]/40">Last updated: August 3, 2026</p>

		<div class="prose-content mt-7 max-w-[640px] text-[0.9375rem] leading-[1.85] text-[var(--ink)]/70">
			<p>
				These Terms of Use govern your access to and use of {SITE_TITLE} (wagelark.com, the
				"Site"). By using the Site, you agree to these terms.
			</p>

			<h2>Content and no professional advice</h2>
			<p>
				WageLark publishes wage, employment, and career-path information sourced primarily from
				the U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics. Content is provided for general informational purposes
				only. It is not personalized career counseling, financial advice, legal advice, or
				immigration advice, and should not be treated as a substitute for consulting a qualified
				professional about your specific situation. We do not endorse or recommend any specific
				employer, school, training program, or certification provider.
			</p>

			<h2>Data accuracy</h2>
			<p>
				We label every wage figure with its source and data year and link back to the original
				government page. Government data is periodically revised and republished (BLS typically
				updates occupational wage data annually); a figure on this Site reflects the most recent
				data available to us as of the "Last updated" date on that page, and may not match the
				current live BLS figures if BLS has since published a newer release. Always check the
				linked source for the most current official figures before relying on a number for an
				important decision.
			</p>

			<h2>Intellectual property</h2>
			<p>
				Unless otherwise noted, the text and original graphics on this Site are owned by WageLark.
				You're welcome to link to our articles or quote brief excerpts with attribution. Republishing
				full articles elsewhere without permission isn't allowed. Underlying BLS government data is
				public domain and not owned by WageLark.
			</p>

			<h2>Third-party links and ads</h2>
			<p>
				The Site may display ads served by advertising partners and may link to third-party sites,
				including government sources. We aren't responsible for the content, accuracy, or practices
				of external sites we link to or that serve ads on this Site. See our
				<a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> for how advertising cookies work.
			</p>

			<h2>No warranty</h2>
			<p>
				The Site is provided "as is" without warranties of any kind. We try to keep articles
				accurate and up to date but make no guarantee that content is complete, current, or free of
				errors.
			</p>

			<h2>Changes</h2>
			<p>
				We may update these terms as the Site evolves. Continued use of the Site after changes take
				effect means you accept the updated terms.
			</p>

			<h2>Contact</h2>
			<p>
				Questions about these terms can be sent to Owen Zhang via the contact information on the
				<a href="/about/">About</a> page.
			</p>
		</div>
	</div>
</Layout>

<style>
	.prose-content :global(h2) {
		margin-top: 1.75rem;
		margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
		font-size: 1.1rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		color: var(--navy);
	}
	.prose-content :global(h2:first-child) {
		margin-top: 0;
	}
	.prose-content :global(p) {
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
	}
	.prose-content :global(a) {
		color: var(--teal-dark);
		text-decoration: underline;
	}
</style>
